title: Continuation prompts advance a thread (Phase 10.5)
story: character-acceptance
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The four frozen continuation-prompt forms each advance the
  active thread exactly one beat through the built bundle; past the last
  beat the conclusion serves and gates the ledger topic. A prompt with
  no active thread falls to the default no-target response.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/character-acceptance/chord/p10-threads.story
    stories/character-acceptance/tests/transcripts/p10-continuation-prompts.transcript

---

# Inert before any thread is active: the default no-target path.
> continue
[OK: contains "Talk to whom?"]

# Before the conclusion, the ledger topic serves its ungated line.
> ask prompter about the ledger
[OK: contains "The ledger keeps its own counsel."]

# The matching ask opens the thread and serves beat 1.
> ask prompter about the shortfall
[OK: contains "It began with a missing shilling."]

# Each frozen prompt form advances exactly one beat.
> tell me more
[OK: contains "Then a missing pound, and nobody blinked."]

> continue
[OK: contains "By Michaelmas the drawer was bare."]

> go on
[OK: contains "And the master's seal was on every receipt."]

# Past the last beat, the conclusion serves.
> and?
[OK: contains "So now you know where the money went."]

# Conclusion is state: the gated ledger line now serves.
> ask prompter about the ledger
[OK: contains "Now that you know the whole of it, read the ledger yourself."]

# A concluded thread never re-engages: prompts are inert again.
> go on
[OK: contains "Talk to whom?"]
